  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ExecuteRPN",
    "file": "imagemagick/MagickCore/fx.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read in ExecuteRPN when evaluating channel-qualified pixel access for expressions like `%[hex:u.intensity]`. In the fU0 path, INTENSITY_CHANNEL is handled by calling GetIntensity(), but then control falls through to the generic channel access block (missing `break`), which indexes `pimg->channel_map[WHICH_NON_ATTR_CHAN].offset`. For `u.intensity`, this qualifier is not a real mapped channel, so the computed offset is invalid and causes an out-of-bounds read from the pixel buffer.",
    "conditions": "Data flow: LABEL coder calls InterpretImageProperties on attacker-controlled filename text; `%[hex:...]` invokes AcquireFxInfo/FxEvaluateChannelExpression multiple times (R/G/B/A channels). With PoC `%[hex:u.intensity]`, ExecuteRPN parses `u.intensity` into fU0 + INTENSITY_CHANNEL and executes the INTENSITY branch. Because of missing `break` after `regA = GetIntensity(...)`, execution continues into generic channel_map indexing, producing an invalid offset and triggering ASan heap-buffer-overflow read. Minimal trigger is a LABEL input containing that property expansion string."
  },
